<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:25Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>El Nino set to intensify before peaking in December, UN warns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c25ed5812a9cd5c26fc92736222d7f6a645826616028c53b071a2ae64eb5dc5</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T06:09:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/environment/20261008-el-nino-set-to-intensify-before-peaking-in-december-un-warns" /><summary type="html">The United Nations warned on Thursday that El Nino will intensify before peaking in December, bringing higher temperatures to much of the planet and compounding the effects of man-made climate change. The World Meteorological Organization added that this naturally occurring weather phenomenon could be the strongest since at least 1950.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Portugal: Cristiano Ronaldo controversy rumbles on</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa32de5e12b65c26e950bc32105d5264e5387244bcffec371f9ed762e61f108f</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T05:35:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261008-portugal-cristiano-ronaldo-controversy-rumbles-on" /><summary type="html">The controversy between Cristiano Ronaldo and Jorge Jesus continues, following the lengthy statement released by the forward on Tuesday. Ronaldo explained his decision to leave the Portugal squad and accused his coach of breaking his word. The affair dominated the headlines in the Portuguese press, overshadowing Portugal’s four Nations League victories. The media are questioning his future while Ronaldo insists he wants to continue playing for the Seleçao.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Live: French high school, university students call for fresh protests as funding demands grow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eb970159918cf13d97916f60db5612db500a3b2a5039780db6e3f01594517f3d</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T03:28:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261008-live-students-fourth-round-protests-education-funding-france" /><summary type="html">French high school and university students were called out to protest again on Thursday, two days after a large turnout demanding more funding, as the government made a series of conciliatory gestures aimed at ending the crisis. Follow our liveblog for all the latest developments.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi Arabia says it will retaliate after deadly Houthi attacks on airports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f80227c97afa91695ab91556f23ec5eb133f358d4e8b28c293b5c2c63c1c9288</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T03:02:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261008-saudi-arabia-strikes-deadly-houthi-attacks-airports" /><summary type="html">Saudi authorities said Wednesday three people were killed and 36 wounded in attacks on Abha and Riyadh’s King Khalid international airports claimed by Yemen’s Iran-backed Houthis. The Saudi-led coalition said it destroyed the ballistic missile launch platform used to attack Riyadh, as fighting with the Houthis intensified across the region.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>DNC sues Trump administration over taxpayer-funded TV ads promoting president</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9625e8e97940aa96e660b977d3409e7ffd13c62073a97db5430b20b44d204adf</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T22:27:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261007-dnc-sues-trump-administration-taxpayer-funded-tv-ads" /><summary type="html">The Democratic National Committee sued President Donald Trump’s administration on Wednesday over taxpayer-funded television ads promoting his political message, alleging illegal government propaganda. The lawsuit seeks to halt federal funding for the ads, which have cost more than $12 million to air ahead of November’s midterm elections, according to AdImpact.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>No longer the same Israel? October 7th and the future of the Jewish State</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ee624bb0fa521a78c6ccd54b8be6acfe448360f8b41bee8180cd1b11b2166e42</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T22:10:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261007-no-longer-the-same-israel-october-7th-and-the-future-of-the-jewish-state" /><summary type="html">For now, it's still Benjamin Netanyahu’s Israel. In 2023, in the immediate aftermath of the country’s worst day of bloodshed in its history, pundits predicted the quick demise of the right wing prime minister. On this the third anniversary of the October Seventh attacks, Israel’s still not reckoned with the security failures on the day, the root causes of the Hamas-led terror attack, the brutal war of vengeance that followed and most of all, Netanyahu’s still prime minister with a fair shot at re-election. Even if the Likud leader’s voted out on October 27th, his most serious general election rivals don't exactly advocate for a radical break when it comes to the Palestinians.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Thousands protest presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro, fearing far-right return in Brazil</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:72aab8b1f307568a7f1ea634f557639a28b80a701c8db1149a0a8cfbf4449b3f</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T22:01:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261007-thousands-protest-flavio-bolsonaro-far-right-brazil" /><summary type="html">Thousands of people joined a student march in downtown Rio de Janeiro on Wednesday to protest against presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro ahead of Brazil's October 25 presidential runoff. Bolsonaro led Sunday's first-round vote, prompting demonstrators to rally behind incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and oppose the far right's return to power.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Israel marks three years since October 7 attack ahead of elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1340d4a7dd8a36cb84727be0dce1279c2058b49b96a291d430b616da125106ee</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T21:50:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261007-israel-three-years-october-7-attack-elections" /><summary type="html">Israel marked the third anniversary of Hamas’s October 7 attack on Wednesday with silent tributes and renewed strikes on Gaza as political debate intensified ahead of elections. Families gathered at the Nova festival site and Kfar Aza kibbutz. Gaza officials said strikes killed five people despite a year-old ceasefire agreement.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>UN health agency wants more details from Russia on suspected pneumonic plague case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c47dac835024d524a03fd72681d3d4373cfb08cc3d9ed8d1c32691b3eb812b9</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T21:24:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/un-health-agency-wants-more-details-from-russia-on-suspected-pneumonic-plague-case" /><summary type="html">A top official with the World Health Organization said Wednesday it doesn’t know how a lab worker in Siberia died, and she urged Russia to provide more information about a case that prompted global concerns about suspected pneumonic plague. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>France suspends stun grenade use at student protests after pupil loses hand</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab133f1cfc9970e0668a1a39d7fa75f762d9425488706fbb434c0357b8d107f5</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T21:19:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-suspends-stun-grenade-use-at-student-protests-after-pupil-loses-hand" /><summary type="html">France has suspended the use of stun grenades by police at student-led demonstrations, the interior minister said Wednesday, as allegations of police brutality mounted after days of sometimes violent demonstrations across the country. Tens of thousands of people took to the streets across France on Tuesday demanding better conditions in high schools. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>French PM vows to address debt despite student protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab3b4b5f1474c2cbf80f43ed2e8203468236fdd171fc58daf8ef2c533dcee16c</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T21:13:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-pm-vows-to-address-debt-despite-student-protests" /><summary type="html">French Prime Minister Sebastien Lecornu has tried to calm both student protesters and jittery bond markets. In an address to the nation, Lecornu stressed that the education ministry had not seen any cuts in last week's budget proposal, but insisted the government must cut its public deficit to 5%. There are growing concerns about France's spending and debt, with the IMF urging the country to "get your house in order." Lecornu also confirmed the release of 10 million barrels of diesel fuel.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Africa joins the data center backlash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6f6f8191ea43a65f9edd35c158c265e066b55334ce3ded77d2826d82b0209ca7</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T20:37:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa-joins-the-data-center-backlash" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, witnesses say Eritrean troops have moved into Ethiopia's Tigray region, but Asmara rejects the reports. Also, the African Union launches the Africa Credit Rating Agency, aiming to assess the financial health of African states and companies. And South African civil society is pushing back against the expansion of data centres  that require vast amounts of electricity, water and land.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>France schools protests: more than 6,000 arrested since start of demonstrations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fa6e703c2f9e044d964bd6145c20db61c3c8d85df904ed6a4b790390e44d7014</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T20:17:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-schools-protests-more-than-6-100-arrested-since-start-of-demonstrations" /><summary type="html">After more than two weeks of high school protests across France, police have arrested a total of 6,100 individuals, the majority of whom are minors who, until now, had no previous criminal record. So, what has happend to these students, and what lies ahead for them? FRANCE 24's Caitlin Brown has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Evicted pensioner who sparked Spain housing protests dies: tenant union</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:615559823439311009e2c4d244a8230e263d32694ce77b77a1016e56bcea6962</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T20:14:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/evicted-pensioner-who-sparked-spain-housing-protests-dies-tenant-union" /><summary type="html">Maricarmen ​Abascal, the 87-year-old woman whose eviction sparked housing ​protests in Spain, has died, Madrid's tenants' union said on Wednesday. Abascal's eviction sparked a series of ​protests ‌across Spain in the past couple ⁠of weeks, including activists camping on one of Madrid's main ‌squares, and calls for tackling a ⁠mounting housing crisis. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid.</summary></entry><entry><title>'It's still unclear whether Netanyahu will pay for what happened during his time in office'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aacb2eb97313fabd2d479a6a0853cc8d9711fc639a839458ff6cbcf1fe62e9ab</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T19:52:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/it-s-still-unclear-whether-netanyahu-will-pay-for-what-happened-during-his-time-in-office" /><summary type="html">As Israel marks the third anniversary of the October 7 attacks, questions linger about the warnings Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu received about them. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Ayala Panievsky, Lecturer at City University of London and author of The New Censorship, explains that the allegations in the run-up to the elections "are very damaging for Netanyahu but there are some factors mitigating the risk for him", including a fragmented opposition as well as the control of major media.</summary></entry><entry><title>White House promotes 'Trump TV' with an AI-altered photo</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0648770bba561aec07edc2ca54f61a2025e3f1180163d5f9ebbb4438b90b8034</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T19:45:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/white-house-promotes-trump-tv-with-an-ai-altered-photo" /><summary type="html">The White House has promoted “Trump TV” using an AI-altered photo of passengers apparently watching the president’s new streaming channel. But the image was originally posted online in February 2023, showing passengers watching the NFL Super Bowl, with one watching the film “Hitch”. The original photo was modified using AI to make it appear the passengers were watching Trump TV. The post did not disclose that the image had been altered. Vedika Bahl explains in Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Evicted pensioner Maricarmen Abascal, heart of Spain's housing protests, dies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:72c8c9ff3ee452d3a88705e924024bd2f361abf55b05f03487c8e3758a5e52d3</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T19:19:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261007-evicted-pensioner-maricarmen-abascal-heart-of-spain-housing-protests-has-died" /><summary type="html">Maricarmen ​Abascal, the 87-year-old woman whose eviction sparked housing ​protests in Spain, has died, Madrid's tenants' union said on Wednesday. Massive protests following Abascal's eviction spiralled into a political crisis, eventually leading Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez to call a snap election.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says 'we don't think' Russian plague is bio-weapon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b19444fef7a12a49f6d16c73e7ce77503990185997a3b68515951ef3dd88560a</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T19:04:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-says-we-don-t-think-russian-plague-is-bio-weapon" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump said Wednesday that the death of a Russian plague laboratory worker did not appear to be linked to a biological weapon. "We don't think so. We're going to find out soon enough, but we don't think so," Trump told reporters in the Oval Office when asked if a "bio-weapon" was involved. Russia warned earlier against "false" information as reports emerged of a second suspected case. The US and UN have urged Russia to be more transparent. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson reports from Washington.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Resilience' of Israelis as they mourn the loss of loved ones and 'the sense that we can be safe'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc8df3ba408288cf6c5cffbdab26d6e5ae7734b8e6ac1d0c095a41f540e75ff0</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T17:46:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261007-resilience-of-israelis-as-they-the-mourn-loss-of-loved-ones-and-the-sense-that-we-can-be-safe" /><summary type="html">Angela Diffley is pleased to welcome Dr. Danny Brom, Founding Director of METIV, the Israel Psychotrauma Center in Jerusalem. According to Dr. Brom, as Israelis and Jewish people around the world continue to mourn the largest loss of Jewish life on a single day since the Holocaust, their fundamental sense of collective security has also been shattered. What strikes him, however, is the resilience that exists alongside the grieving. How can individuals, communities and society rebuild a sense of safety without allowing fear to dictate the future? Yet, as Dr. Brom observes, “the war is still going on,” while political leaders speak of pursuing “the ultimate victory, which no one really knows what that is.”</summary></entry><entry><title>France summons Iranian ambassador over 'disinformation' on student protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4835fab91f21c1eebe26079864fb4dec4f745571ddf9430f805dc2b174922ae7</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T17:23:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261007-france-summons-iranian-ambassador-over-disinformation-on-student-protests" /><summary type="html">The French foreign ministry on Wednesday summoned the Iranian ambassador to protest against a "disinformation campaign conducted by the Iranian authorities" over the student protests that have rocked France. The move came a day after Tehran summoned the French ambassador over the treatment of protesters in France.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>France suspends the use of stun grenades after student protester loses hand</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d9df9873c205b9987ee438d957813b1801c1ac5973248c1ceba42caf457e29bb</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T17:05:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261007-france-suspends-the-use-of-stun-grenades-after-student-protester-loses-hand" /><summary type="html">The French ​government said Wednesday it would suspend the use of stun grenades in its attempts to manage the student protests now roiling the country after a 15-year-old boy had his hand blown off during a clash with riot police.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>What France's student protesters want – and what the government is offering</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2b4f949d6ebbd3883c270d298753a83952c2f42b461d69d0c58ab1e7d20e0fe</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T16:41:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261007-what-france-s-student-protesters-want-%E2%80%93-and-what-the-government-is-offering" /><summary type="html">Staff shortages, rats in the corridors, and a university admissions system that feels like a lottery: As protests sweep France, high school students have drawn up a list of demands to deal with these and other issues. Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu has promised a government response by the end of October, but whether he can quell the unrest remains to be seen.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>France: Government suspends stun grenade use in school protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9559007b041bd1bd6efc85dd9dc5e29d5c1c0bc6ddfd69a85471e907d78c786f</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T16:15:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261007-france-government-suspends-stun-grenade-use-in-school-protests" /><summary type="html">France has suspended police use of stun grenades at high school demonstrations, the interior minister announced, amid growing allegations of police brutality after two weeks of protests marked by frequent violent clashes that have left hundreds injured.France has suspended police use of stun grenades at high school demonstrations, the interior minister announced, amid growing allegations of police brutality after two weeks of protests marked by frequent violent clashes that have left hundreds injured.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: France summons Iranian ambassador over 'disinformation' on student protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba595ea8201ab28801f58014dbd6ba00f9ddc95cc842decbcade51205978bed6</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T15:52:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261007-middle-east-live-houthis-target-airport-in-yemen-as-israel-marks-october-7-anniversary" /></entry></feed>
